        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does Home Depot sell treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes, on homedepot.com. When we checked on 18 October 2026, its Treadmills category held 54 treadmills by its own filter, all from little-known budget brands such as LIVACA, Flynama, Tidoin and COWLOWN. Every listing we sampled was online-only, for delivery or ship-to-store pickup.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Home Depot have treadmills in store?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not as stocked items. Every treadmill listing we sampled was marked online-only, with ship-to-home or ship-to-store fulfilment. Ship-to-store means you collect a boxed machine at the store, not that you can try one there.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Home Depot sell NordicTrack, ProForm or Sole treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not when we checked. Site searches on 18 October 2026 for NordicTrack, ProForm, Sole, Horizon, Bowflex, Sunny Health & Fitness and XTERRA returned no treadmills from those brands. For those, look at the manufacturer, a sporting goods or specialty store, or other big retailers.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the Home Depot return policy on treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              When we read it on 18 October 2026, most merchandise had 90 days with proof of purchase, and the treadmill listings we sampled were marked 90-day returnable. Items too large to bring to a store can be picked up if eligible, after a call to customer care. Check the listing and current policy before buying.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Home Depot assemble treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We found no treadmill assembly option. The category's In-Home Installation Available filter returned only a cat exercise wheel when we checked. Plan to assemble the treadmill yourself or hire a local assembler.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are Home Depot treadmills any good?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Some may suit light walking, but the listings we read had short warranties, mostly one to three months, and specification tables that often disagreed with their titles. For a machine you plan to use for years, buy an established brand with a published frame, motor and parts warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
